* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.onnx binary

# examples/giant_props/ is stored byte-for-byte. Do NOT normalise it.
#
# The tree is mixed on purpose and the mix is load-bearing: 13 files are
# genuinely CRLF, several tools hash them, and a CRLF shebang makes a .sh
# fail under bash (found and fixed once already in
# sumo_gyro_platform/authoring/mix_call_audio.sh). This directory has no
# history before this commit, so every integrity claim in it rests on sha256
# comparison; a checkout that silently flipped line endings would change
# every one of those hashes while changing no content, making real drift
# indistinguishable from noise.
examples/giant_props/** -text
